{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:26:17.725Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5b9b19bbbc8191a2b851e61875cb5c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_b6uvr8Nc3dc4T1637XQAtqJI","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"wc -l /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/CODEX-RESTART-HANDOVER-2026-07-12.md && sed -n '1,260p' /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:26:17.885Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75d5-dd1d-7822-8066-9ab0a1f993b7","call_id":"call_b6uvr8Nc3dc4T1637XQAtqJI","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"     445 /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md\n     527 /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/CODEX-RESTART-HANDOVER-2026-07-12.md\n     972 total\n# Entire Brain and Brain Bench handover\n\nStatus: authoritative operational handover as of 2026-07-18 (Europe/Paris).\n\nThis document replaces the dated execution handovers and state snapshots now\npreserved under [`outdated/2026-07-18/`](outdated/2026-07-18/). It describes the\ncurrent product candidate, the benchmark work that actually exists, the evidence\nthat may be claimed, and the order in which work should resume.\n\n## 1. Read order and authority\n\nUse these sources in this order:\n\n1. **This handover** for live branches, pull requests, results, blockers, and\n   next actions.\n2. [The active benchmark and product-improvement goal](ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md)\n   for the terminal completion contract. Its mission and three co-primary\n   endpoints remain authoritative; dated checkpoint sections inside it are\n   historical unless this handover repeats them.\n3. The relevant committed artifacts in `entire-brain` or `brain-bench` for any\n   individual measurement. A prose summary never overrides its source artifact.\n4. [The master plan](master-plan.md) for the longer cross-repository roadmap.\n5. [The paper workspace](paper/entire-toolchain/README.md) for frozen research\n   evidence and carefully bounded historical claims. It is not a live branch\n   handoff.\n\nDocuments under `outdated/` are provenance only. Do not use their “current,”\n“next,” or branch-state wording as present tense.\n\n### Terminology\n\nThe product formerly named `entire-sem` is now **Entire Graph**, with repository\nand current command surface `entire-graph` / `entire graph`. Frozen benchmark\nartifacts and exact historical treatment labels retain `entire-sem` where that\nwas the name actually executed. Renaming an old artifact would break provenance.\n\n## 2. Terminal goal\n\nThe program is not complete when the harness is merely runnable, when retrieval\nmetrics improve, or when one scenario becomes faster. It must both build a\ncausally credible benchmark **and** use that benchmark as a control loop to\nimprove Entire Brain.\n\nThe final powered comparison must show practically meaningful, statistically\ndefensible gains across all three co-primary dimensions, without a material\ncross-dimension regression:\n\n1. end-to-end elapsed time to a validated coding result;\n2. model-token cost for that result; and\n3. downstream code quality.\n\nThe primary user-value comparison is final optimized `retrieved_memory` versus\ntreatment-neutral `no_memory`. The product-progress comparison is final optimized\nEntire Brain versus a content-addressed pre-optimization Entire Brain baseline.\nBoth are required. Scenario diagnostics, packet bytes, local latency, allocations,\nand retrieval hit rates guide iteration but do not by themselves satisfy the\nterminal goal.\n\n## 3. Executive state\n\n| Repository / lane | Authoritative checkout | Branch and head | Remote state | Pull request |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Entire Brain integration | `/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/benchmark-repair-integration/entire-brain` | `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` at `923b8a915925967c8ee1ffab3ff603f688a5427b` | clean and pushed | [entire-brain#75](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/75), draft, open, **conflicting** |\n| Entire Brain ordinary checkout | `/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain` | old WIP at `bbe1bdf5` | not the integration candidate | none; do not resume product work here |\n| Brain Bench agentic pilot | `/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot` | `codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` at `d2f13dc15a54b84a954226ab9df76e0086676d99` | clean and pushed | [brain-bench#34](https://github.com/entirehq/brain-bench/pull/34), draft, open, mergeable; fresh CI in progress |\n| Brain Bench ordinary checkout | `/Users/thomi/Projects/brain-bench` | `feat/core-bench-spike` at local `ab07c160696127a537e3ca90e94713b2383f5b7c` | clean but local tracking state is stale; remote branch is `1b10614a10fa8b670f324b607efa3e5f00cd6239` | not the current session lane |\n| Entire Graph retrieval candidate | `/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph` | `codex/improve-search-retrieval` at `3928dcc7bffd4c9b16324bd2707e311d5944456d` | clean and pushed | [entire-graph#43](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/43), ready, mergeable, all seven checks green |\n\nLive remote bases at the handover:\n\n- Entire Brain `main`: `bc0203b761cbc500bfcb0acff723dad57ae37770`.\n- Brain Bench `main`: `da189c95dd94fa18612e268639a2262bd02735c2`.\n- Entire Graph `main`: `fafe92878b5e920fe161d8078ee91762fe33e9b4`.\n\n## 4. Entire Brain integration candidate\n\n### 4.1 Branch and PR state\n\nPR #75 is 120 commits ahead of and 83 commits behind live `main`. GitHub reports\nthe branch as conflicting, and the comparison is large enough that its API file\nlist truncates at 300. Cursor Bugbot is green at `923b8a91`; that does not replace\nthe required reconciliation and post-reconciliation test pass.\n\nThe current PR body still says 116 commits ahead. The live comparison above is\nthe authoritative value and the PR description should be refreshed after the\nbranch is reconciled.\n\nThe final four integrated commits are:\n\n| Commit | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `08f30453` | Gate action guidance on relevant history instead of emitting noisy actions. |\n| `97d58824` | Recover operational edit targets from Git intent. |\n| `76e75b48` | Rank semantic test suggestions for likely edit/test relevance. |\n| `923b8a91` | Preserve treatment isolation when a private semantic-synthesis stream is present but empty. |\n\nFable 5 reviewed the source checkpoint `60b3269e` for the first three changes and\nreported no blocker. An independent combined review then found the\npresent-empty/private-stream isolation defect; `923b8a91` fixed it, added a\nregression test, and passed re-review with no remaining finding.\n\n### 4.2 Validation at `923b8a91`\n\n- Combined focused tests passed.\n- Combined focused race tests passed.\n- The deadline-sensitive Git-intent case passed five isolated runs out of five.\n- `go test ./... -count=1` passed; `internal/cli` took 99.533 seconds.\n- `go vet ./...` passed.\n- `git diff --check 9193b404..HEAD` passed.\n- No paid/provider, private-log, or holdout benchmark was run for this final\n  Entire Brain integration.\n\nThese validations predate reconciliation with live `main` and must be repeated\nafter conflicts are resolved.\n\n### 4.3 Product results that may be claimed\n\nThe measurements below are development diagnostics. They use different\nscenarios and are **not additive**.\n\n| Change / scenario | Relevance or quality result | Time result | Packet / token result | Claim boundary |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Legacy history ranking | Exact ranking preserved | 471 ms to 117 ms steady state (`-75.2%`) | Allocated bytes `-99.93%`; packet bytes preserved | Local recurring-history path only |\n| Stale-index bridge | Two real post-index implementation/test targets absent to rank #1 / #1 | About 13.4 ms added | `+88` compact bytes | Two targeted stale-index cases |\n| Semantic-root dedupe | Same useful roots after dedupe | Not a primary measure | Exact `o200k_base` tokens `-13.73%` pooled over two real packets | Packet-level evidence only |\n| Action relevance gate | False action guidance 11 to 0 | Not a primary measure | JSON 14,097 to 10,742 bytes (`-23.80%`) | Exact-symbol file ranking still misses |\n| Git-intent overlay: installer | `scripts/install.sh` absent to edit rank #1 | Overlay stayed within a 100 ms fail-closed budget; observed about 15–21 ms across local cases | JSON 47,752 to 46,992 (`-1.59%`) | Tests unchanged |\n| Git-intent overlay: Windows CI | `.github/workflows/test.yml` to rank #1 | Same bounded overlay | JSON 35,268 to 33,760 (`-4.28%`) | Tests unchanged |\n| Git-intent overlay: inherited CGO | `mise.toml` to rank #1 | Same bounded overlay | JSON 42,665 to 43,188 (`+1.23%`) | Small byte regression accepted for recovered target |\n| Git-intent overlay: macOS warning | `mise.toml` to rank #1 | Same bounded overlay | JSON 42,765 to 43,337 (`+1.34%`) | Small byte regression accepted for recovered target |\n| Suggestion ranking, preserved eight-task corpus | Manual Hit@8 0/8 to 6/8; one abstention and one miss | 0.78–0.97 ms per 1k suggestions; 6.2–11.7 ms per 10k; 21 allocations | Compact bytes 171,767 to 161,313 (`-6.09%`); exact tokens 51,733 to 49,224 (`-4.85%`) | Prior judgment map was not persisted; do not present as a freshly reproduced result |\n\nThe exact eight-task SQLite snapshots still exist, but a no-write replay cannot\nopen them because SQLite readers require writable WAL/SHM sidecars. The snapshots\nwere deliberately not mutated to manufacture a rerun.\n\n### 4.4 Product gaps still open\n\n1. Exact-symbol cases can still select the wrong implementation/test files.\n2. A raw-history zero-match fallback can scan about 392.7 MB, taking about\n   4.37 seconds of a roughly 5.07-second brief.\n3. `compact_v3` remains opt-in, so its savings are not the default product\n   experience.\n4. PR #75 must be reconciled with 83 commits from `main`; conflicts and semantic\n   drift are unknown until that work is done.\n5. The eight-task suggestion judgment map needs a durable, reviewable format if\n   the result is to be reproduced rather than cited as preserved development\n   evidence.\n\n### 4.5 Important lineage boundary\n\nThe benchmark-gate lineage through the current integration includes these\nmilestones:\n\n`bbe1bdf5` → `00642c67` → `1e5c95aa` → `ca8a08c4` → `157f805b` →\n`f319e954` → `1c39aeb2` → `e9cbc7aa` → `f0552070` → `b47dc5bc` →\n`87acd380` → `ac3d11a2` → `9193b404` → `923b8a91`.\n\nAfter `ac3d11a2`, `fcb444eb` froze the non-executing run-storage contract before\nthe later product commits.\n\nThe separate opt-in Agent V1/V2 commits `65880f5d`, `856bcff3`, `3329d054`,\n`cfb43d66`, `31b7d0d7`, `86f0d70d`, `9789ae7b`, and `77ace7bd` are **not\nancestors of `923b8a91`**. Do not claim that PR #75 contains them. They remain\nindependent development evidence until deliberately reconciled and retested.\n\n## 5. Entire Brain benchmark readiness\n\nThe benchmark work is substantial, but the system is intentionally not\nauthorized to execute the frozen confirmatory schedule.\n\nWhat exists on the integration lineage:\n\n- content-addressed engine, treatment, task, prompt, schedule, pricing, and\n  evidence contracts;\n- fail-closed task validity and treatment-isolation checks;\n- temporal eligibility before ranking;\n- counterbalanced scheduling and cache-policy contracts;\n- negative-control classification and receipts;\n- three-endpoint confirmatory analysis with clustered uncertainty and\n  intersection-union success semantics;\n- a frozen 248-attempt schedule binding.\n\nWhat the frozen run-storage contract actually permits:\n\n- build and check only;\n- no model/provider execution and no run mutation;\n- runtime locators remain null;\n- the owner trust root remains empty;\n- approved cache material is still pending;\n- no staging, executor, approval, or candidate-binding path is complete.\n\nNo attempt from the 248-attempt schedule ran. The APFS issue is not disk\nfullness: macOS reported about 191.9 GB available for important use, above the\n16 GiB planning threshold. The open issue is a trusted APFS-aware observer plus\nbounded reservation and cleanup attestation. Do not delete caches or claim a\ncapacity blocker based on immediately unallocated `df` blocks.\n\n## 6. Brain Bench state\n\n### 6.1 Current session lane: PR #34\n\nThe session’s Brain Bench work is the clean, pushed\n`codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` branch at `d2f13dc`, not the ordinary\n`feat/core-bench-spike` checkout. It contains 30 commits on top of `89ef74f` and\nis stacked on `codex/graph-v7-evidence`.\n\nPR #34 adds and repairs a three-repository, three-treatment agent-native coding\npilot. It compares native file tools, Entire Graph retrieval, and the full CBM\nsurface in isolated checkouts, recording edits, tests, transcripts, usage, cost,\ntiming, and reference-patch alignment. This was a paid/provider-backed\n**development pilot using Claude Opus**. It was not a frozen candidate,\nprivate-holdout, or publication-authorized run. Do not conflate it with the\nno-provider final Entire Brain A/B described above.\n\nThe PR description is stale: it documents the initial diagnostic and 42 tests,\nbut not the corrected pilot, later replay, or Tasks smoke. The committed\nevidence documents `corrected-pilot-20260718.md` and\n`graph-retrieval-replay-20260718.md` are the current completed-run record.\n\n`7463d3ad` freezes a retained Tasks smoke slice: 18 questions\nwith controller-only expected answers and scoring specifications across\n`spf13/cobra`, `reduxjs/redux-toolkit`, and `django/django`. Selection is\ndeterministic and outcome-blind, with Entire-owned and prior\nrepair-development repositories excluded. `d2f13dc` adds the live Claude\nharness and scorer. The design groups six questions into one conversation per\nrepository and treatment, for nine Claude Opus attempts.\n\nA separate, pre-existing Codex lane started that live run at 12:36:05 CEST on\n2026-07-18 with three workers, model `opus`, 24 turns, a 1,200-second timeout,\nand a maximum reported budget of $5 per attempt. Its output directory is\n`/private/tmp/graph-agentic-tasks-smoke-20260718`. This documentation task did\nnot start or authorize it. At this handover checkpoint the process was active\nand no completed result set was available. This is development execution, not\nEntire Brain confirmatory or holdout execution.\n\nThe new scorer is not ready to support a rankable claim. At `d2f13dc` it branches\non `expected.kind` instead of each case’s `scoring.mode`, does not score snippet\ncontent, collapses code-search scoring to definition name/path matching, and\ndoes not eligibility-gate aggregate exact rate on treatment compliance. Repair\nand independently review those semantics with unpaid fixtures. Quarantine the\nin-progress outputs as diagnostic raw attempts; do not interpret the aggregate\nor launch paid retries before scorer/protocol review.\n\n### 6.2 Corrected pilot results\n\n| Treatment | Eligible acceptance | Raw acceptance |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Entire Graph | 1/3 | 1/3 |\n| CBM | 1/3 | 1/3 |\n| Native file tools | 0/3 | 1/3 |\n\nEntire Graph used fewer output tokens, tool calls, elapsed time, and reported\ncost in this tiny development sample, but it **did not win correctness**. The\nlater two-case Graph retrieval replay recorded controller acceptance of 0/2.\nThe VS Code result is a genuine behavioral failure. The Vite repair may be\nbehaviorally equivalent, but its bound future test calls a reference-only\nhelper, so that result remains a scorer-validity question rather than an\nestablished behavioral failure. Subsequent retrieval work improved target ranks\nin diagnostics only; no later paid replay of those two repair cases was made.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
