{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:26:29.510Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5b9b258088819199de8d028f6e1cba","status":"completed","call_id":"call_VbbGV531JeQH1X6ZoyCHZ5X5","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '261,520p' /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:26:29.674Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75d6-0b2a-7da1-a866-e08fa7b8dd11","call_id":"call_VbbGV531JeQH1X6ZoyCHZ5X5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"The separate Tasks smoke described above was still running. Three repositories\nand a two-case replay are useful for debugging, not for a broad product claim.\n\nGraph V8 still authorizes no catalog, ranking, scoring, or publication.\n\n### 6.3 CI state\n\nThe CI run for `d2f13dc` was in progress when this handover was updated. The\nimmediately preceding run at `fee870b7` was red:\n\n- 2,331 tests passed;\n- 6 tests skipped;\n- 1 test failed.\n\nThe failing inherited frozen V8 toolchain closure expects the\n`graph_v8_ranking_worker.py` hash prefix `6e80…`, while the inherited current\nbytes have prefix `b328…`. PR #31 exhibits the same inherited mismatch. Treat\nthis as a closure/reconciliation problem unless the fresh run establishes a\ndifferent cause. An in-progress rerun is not green evidence.\n\n### 6.4 Ordinary checkout and remote main\n\n`/Users/thomi/Projects/brain-bench` is clean at local `ab07c160` on\n`feat/core-bench-spike`, but its upstream view is stale. The live remote branch\nhead is `1b10614a`; live `main` is `da189c95`. Before reusing this checkout,\nfetch explicitly and decide whether the intended work belongs on PR #34 or a\nnew branch based on current `main`.\n\n## 7. Entire Graph dependency state\n\nEntire Graph PR #43 is ready and mergeable at `3928dcc7`; its Linux, macOS, and\nWindows builds/tests plus lint are green. It improves coding-agent retrieval via\nsparse fusion and causal-neighborhood expansion.\n\nAt that commit, the live capability inventory is:\n\n- 185 supported language/filetype labels;\n- 36 semantic languages;\n- 149 inventory-only language/filetype labels;\n- 205 deterministic extensions/suffixes.\n\nThese are capability-inventory counts, not proof that all semantic languages\nparse real repositories cleanly. Historical top-30 trust tiers remain benchmark\nevidence, while [language-tiers.md](language-tiers.md) now keeps only the stable\ntier model and links here for live counts.\n\n## 8. Ordered next moves\n\n### Move 1 — reconcile the Entire Brain candidate\n\n1. Work only in\n   `/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/benchmark-repair-integration/entire-brain`.\n2. Fetch live `main`, inspect the full 83-commit divergence, and create an\n   explicit conflict map before editing.\n3. Reconcile in reviewable slices. Preserve benchmark fail-closed contracts and\n   isolate generated evidence/corpora from product-path conflicts.\n4. Rerun focused tests after each slice, then full tests, race coverage for\n   touched concurrency paths, vet, and diff checks.\n5. Refresh PR #75’s divergence, validation, and residual-risk text.\n\nThis move is first because all further Entire Brain product work on the current\ncandidate compounds an already large conflict surface.\n\n### Move 2 — resume the product scenario loop\n\nAfter reconciliation is green, iterate on actual user-facing failures:\n\n1. Fix exact-symbol implementation/test selection and add a frozen regression\n   scenario.\n2. Profile the 392.7 MB raw-history zero-match scan; add a safe prefilter,\n   bounded index, or cached negative result without changing ranking semantics.\n3. Measure every change against both pre-optimization Entire Brain and the\n   current candidate: target relevance, local elapsed time, allocations, packet\n   bytes, exact tokenizer count, and downstream test outcome where available.\n4. Reject or revise changes that move one dimension by hiding a material loss in\n   another.\n5. Promote `compact_v3` only after compatibility and parity evidence supports a\n   default change.\n\nThe output of this loop is product improvement with benchmark evidence—not more\nharness surface for its own sake.\n\n### Move 3 — close the Brain Bench development branch\n\n1. Reconcile PR #34’s inherited V8 closure against its base and PR #31; do not\n   silently bless new bytes by changing a hash without explaining provenance.\n2. Review and fix the replay’s Vite future-test validity and the new smoke\n   scorer’s mode-specific and treatment-compliance semantics before another\n   paid run.\n3. Update the PR description with the corrected 3×3 pilot, the nuanced replay,\n   the in-progress/non-rankable Tasks smoke, exact claim boundaries, and current\n   test counts.\n4. Run the unpaid regression suite and get CI green.\n5. Decide whether to land the pilot tooling as development infrastructure while\n   keeping Graph V8 catalog/rank/score/publication authority false.\n\n### Move 4 — complete unpaid benchmark gates\n\n1. Finish unpaid fixtures and independent review for the new Tasks smoke runner\n   and scorer. Quarantine the in-progress raw attempts and do not launch retries\n   or further paid cells without explicit budget authorization.\n2. Expand the representative development task population beyond three\n   repositories; keep development, negative-control, and holdout identities\n   disjoint.\n3. Finish trusted run-storage, cache binding, APFS-aware resource observation,\n   reservation, cleanup, executor, reversal, and approval contracts.\n4. Freeze candidate/product identities only after PR #75 is reconciled and the\n   next product loop settles.\n5. Run synthetic, no-provider, and negative-control validations first.\n6. Recalculate power and freeze practical-effect thresholds before any holdout\n   is opened.\n\n### Move 5 — confirmatory execution only with explicit authority\n\nNo confirmatory model/provider, private-data, or holdout run should start merely\nbecause the code can execute it. Require an explicit candidate, frozen design,\nvalidated resources, owner approval, and budget authorization. Report all three\nco-primary endpoints and critical strata; failure of any endpoint means another\nproduct-improvement cycle, not a redefinition of success.\n\n## 9. Working guardrails\n\n- Keep benchmark construction and Entire Brain improvement co-primary.\n- Show user-facing Entire Brain results early; do not substitute test counts or\n  harness volume for product outcomes.\n- Use sub-agents for bounded review, reconciliation, and scenario work, then\n  independently verify their changes.\n- Commit and push coherent checkpoints regularly.\n- Do not run paid benchmarks without explicit authorization.\n- Do not access holdout/private data to diagnose development failures.\n- Preserve frozen artifact bytes and historical `entire-sem` labels.\n- Keep unrelated dirty-worktree changes intact.\n- Disk capacity is not presently a blocker; do not delete user caches to create\n  space.\n\n## 10. Documentation and archive map\n\nThe live planning surface is deliberately small:\n\n- this handover;\n- the active goal;\n- the master plan;\n- `lat-md-comparison.md`;\n- `language-tiers.md`;\n- the paper workspace and immutable evidence it explicitly identifies.\n\nSuperseded root plans, dated handovers, old state snapshots, and old benchmark\nrepair documents are indexed in\n[`outdated/2026-07-18/README.md`](outdated/2026-07-18/README.md). Superseded paper\nplans and reviews are indexed in\n[`outdated/paper-entire-toolchain/README.md`](outdated/paper-entire-toolchain/README.md).\n\n## 11. Resume commands\n\nInspect the Entire Brain candidate:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/benchmark-repair-integration/entire-brain\ngit status --short\ngit fetch origin\ngit rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD\ngh pr view 75 --repo entireio/entire-brain --web\n```\n\nInspect the Brain Bench pilot:\n\n```bash\ncd /private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\ngit status --short\ngit fetch origin\ngh pr checks 34 --repo entirehq/brain-bench\ngh pr view 34 --repo entirehq/brain-bench --web\n```\n\nInspect the Entire Graph dependency:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\ngit status --short\ngit fetch origin\ngh pr checks 43 --repo entireio/entire-graph\n```\n\nNone of these inspection commands authorizes a paid run, holdout access, branch\nintegration, or merge.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
