{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:27:21.430Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5b9b5970ec8191b7ca8fa3d807f47c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_rOdzhJJQ7nU6DmtiMg8dy4ee","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"wc -l /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md && rg -n '^#|^##|Entire Graph|Graph|repository|disjoint|preregister|freeze|paid|authorization|smoke|task population' /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md | head -260\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":16000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:27:21.606Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75d6-d606-7e51-a2ac-b680c3163808","call_id":"call_rOdzhJJQ7nU6DmtiMg8dy4ee","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"     926 /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md\n1:# Entire Brain benchmark and product-improvement goal\n15:three-repository Claude Opus pilot is diagnostic only: Entire Graph used fewer output tokens, tools,\n19:three-repository Tasks smoke whose nine-attempt Opus run was started by a separate pre-existing Codex\n20:lane at 12:36 CEST while this documentation audit was in progress. Its scoring semantics require unpaid\n34:## 1. Mission\n51:## 2. Required final comparisons\n55:### 2.1 User-value comparison\n62:### 2.2 Product-progress comparison\n72:## 3. Non-negotiable completion contract\n84:4. The task population is representative across repositories, task families, difficulty, answerable\n103:## 4. Co-primary endpoint contract\n105:The final numeric floors are frozen only after unpaid development calibration and before the holdout\n111:### 4.1 Elapsed time\n125:### 4.2 Token cost\n136:### 4.3 Code quality\n148:## 5. Statistical decision rule\n168:- no-material-regression bounds for critical task, repository, and cache-state strata.\n173:## 6. Benchmark-to-product optimization loop\n179:2. Run or reuse unpaid deterministic/retrieval diagnostics and authorized development cells only.\n195:## 7. Execution plan\n197:### Phase A — trustworthy measurement substrate\n203:- Keep the holdout unopened and run no paid model cells.\n208:### Phase B — three-dimensional metric and instrumentation contract\n219:### Phase C — representative development population and baselines\n230:### Phase D — product-improvement sprints\n241:### Phase E — freeze and confirm\n243:- Recompute power from development-only calibration; freeze tasks, repetitions, effects, endpoint\n246:- Obtain explicit owner authorization for the paid run.\n253:### Phase F — ship and reproduce\n262:## 8. Current execution slice\n269:`pending_owner_authorization`. No private replay or publication approval is implied. The active slice\n278:3. obtain explicit authorization for a one-time safe export of the 14 development queries and their\n282:5. freeze owner-approved practical floors and strictly better planning alternatives, gather\n287:No paid/model cell, protected-query export, default switch, or holdout access is implied by the first\n290:## 9. First measurement-driven product queue\n295:### 9.1 Repair the measurement boundary\n305:### 9.2 Profile and condition the raw-history fallback\n317:### 9.3 Compact the agent packet\n327:### 9.4 Re-evaluate locus-scoped fact retrieval behind a development flag\n332:authenticated corpus and the expanded task population, keep the existing flat arm as control, and\n336:### 9.5 Queue order\n349:### 9.6 Initial profiler smoke result and revised hypotheses\n351:The opt-in profiler landed at integration commit `07e36d86`. An unpaid smoke run used one checked-in\n373:1. complete the 114-unique-prompt, three-repository unpaid profile and content-address its inputs;\n382:No smoke-run number is a product claim. Queue order remains subject to the full development profile,\n386:### 9.7 Full development profile baseline\n391:outside the repository at mode 0600; it contains hashes and numeric telemetry only. Its frozen\n398:First-observation baseline by repository:\n419:authorize opening the holdout, paid model calls, publication, or a default product-format switch.\n421:### 9.8 First product sprint result: direct FTS history hydration\n458:### 9.9 Compact-v1 full development A/B result\n485:### 9.10 First guarded facts-quality probe and prerequisite\n502:authorization has been recorded, and no real query IDs, texts, or policies were added.\n511:### 9.11 Compact-v2 clears the fixed packet-cost gate\n535:No task grew; the minimum per-task byte reduction was 14.4682%. All three repository medians cleared\n544:paid/model trial, or authorize changing the MCP/CLI default.\n546:### 9.12 Power-v4 evidence contract is implemented; authenticated sizing remains pending\n557:the complete task population and review ledger, binds the complete selected universe and relations in\n559:binds per-cell provider/CLI/requested-and-resolved-model/timeout identity, freezes the production\n568:harness tests pass at `e322f93d`. No provider/model invocation, private/holdout opening, or paid run was\n571:### 9.13 Development task inventory and negative controls are real but not yet reviewed tasks\n589:symptom/leakage/scope checks, source lineages are pairwise disjoint, repository commitments validate,\n598:### 9.14 Offline relevance arithmetic is available but cannot authorize a product choice\n605:metadata or self-declared producer identities cannot turn them into an authorization.\n608:fixture still requires the existing safe-export authorization path. A later authoritative evaluator\n612:### 9.15 Next product candidate: trust-preserving adaptive packet foundation\n645:### 9.16 Expanded multi-repository development inventory is frozen and integrated\n649:`codex/benchmark-repair-integration`. It binds exact Git, repository, remote/ref, 31-first-parent\n657:| Entire Graph | 19 | 6 / 3 / 10 |\n673:all 14 frozen files, passed all four repository-bound checks, and ran 19 focused tests in 61.644\n677:or paid benchmark.\n679:### 9.17 Stage 1 freezes the six-arm packet tradeoff surface\n712:### 9.18 Agent-v1 pressure precursor freezes the local cost defect\n717:behavior change. Four deterministic fixtures freeze the ordinary rich packet (2,486 bytes),\n739:### 9.19 Product slice A removes the profiled-path double build\n759:### 9.20 Product slice B packs agent packets incrementally\n792:### 9.20a Agent V2 is privacy-audited, pushed, and still opt-in\n807:### 9.21 Multi-repository negative-control execution is planned, not authorized\n813:It freezes all 62 ordered candidates, baseline before first-parent source reversal, two repetitions per\n815:It also freezes an 8 GiB staging ceiling plus an 8 GiB reserve, so execution requires evidence of at\n819:`pending_owner_authorization` and the checked tool exposes only deterministic `build` and `check`\n824:repository/candidate reorderings that the runtime checker rejected. The repaired implementation pins\n825:those dependencies and embeds an exact generated schema projection of all three repository rows and\n850:holdout, or paid run occurred. Calibration/holdout membership, population assignment, and all execution\n853:### 9.22 Historical 2026-07-17 proposed sequence and blockers\n860:The unpaid work proposed at that checkpoint was:\n870:   explicit authorization; do not regenerate the inventory from outcomes.\n882:   commitment-only holdout and freeze the canonical protocol before requesting any fixed-cell paid\n897:## 10. Guardrails and authorization boundaries\n899:- Do not open or derive the fresh holdout before protocol freeze.\n900:- Do not run paid model benchmarks without explicit owner authorization and a passing pricing/budget\n910:## 11. Owner decisions still required before confirmatory freeze\n912:Development can continue without these decisions, but confirmatory freeze cannot:\n920:- approve the independently reviewed task population and commitment-only calibration/holdout split;\n926:- authorize the one-time paid holdout execution.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
