{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:30:22.054Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f75d9-96e6-7f53-8bcb-5b8ed8b21eb9","author":"/root/plan_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan_audit\nPayload:\nRead-only audit complete; `/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan` remains clean. I did not inspect protected real V7 identities, queries, qrels, answers, ranks, scores, or outcomes.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- The authoritative operational source is the [2026-07-18 handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:12); archived plans are historical provenance only ([README](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/README.md:76)).\n- The current Entire Graph candidate is `3928dcc7...`, but it is not documented as a confirmatory/V8 freeze ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:61)).\n- Graph V8 currently authorizes no cataloging, ranking, scoring, or publication ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:264)).\n- V8 toolchain closure is broken: the expected ranking-worker hash prefix is `6e80…`, while inherited bytes are `b328…`; provenance must be reconciled against the base and PR #31 ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:275)).\n- No live `entire-plan` document defines a complete V8 manifest, protocol hash, exact V8 repository/test-set commitment, exact frozen Graph/Brain heads, or V8 thresholds. Those must resolve to committed Brain Bench artifacts, not be inferred from archived V7 plans ([README](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/README.md:55)).\n\nThe currently documented predefined development set is the retained 18-question Tasks smoke at `7463d3ad`: controller-only expected answers and scoring specifications across three public repositories, selected deterministically and outcome-blind while excluding Entire-owned and prior repair-development repositories ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:221)). It is not V8 authority. Its scorer requires unpaid semantic repair and independent fixture review before any rankable claim ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:237)).\n\nLive preregistration requirements are:\n\n- Expand and independently validate representative development tasks while keeping the holdout sealed ([goal](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md:219)).\n- Freeze tasks, repetitions, effects, endpoint rules, aggregation, K, engines, runner/model, prices, schedule, holdout commitment, budget, and protocol hash before execution ([goal](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md:241)).\n- Keep development, negative-control, and holdout identities disjoint ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:357)).\n- Freeze product identities only after Brain PR #75 is reconciled and product iteration settles ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:367)).\n\nRemaining non-paid work:\n\n1. Reconcile V8 toolchain bytes with the base/PR #31, document provenance, run unpaid regressions, and obtain green CI while preserving false V8 authority.\n2. Fix scorer mode dispatch, snippet scoring, code-search semantics, and treatment-compliance eligibility; add fixtures and independent review; quarantine existing attempts.\n3. Expand the development population beyond three repositories; pre-record expected answers/scoring; enforce deterministic outcome-blind selection, contamination review, and development/negative-control/holdout disjointness.\n4. Reconcile Brain PR #75, repeat focused/full/race/vet/diff validation, and complete the product scenario loop before freezing exact product heads.\n5. Finish trusted storage, actual cache binding, APFS-aware observation/reservation/cleanup, staging, executor, first-parent reversal, interruption behavior, candidate binding, and approval contracts ([handover](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:184)).\n6. Run synthetic, no-provider, and negative-control validations.\n7. Recalculate power from development-only data and freeze practical effects and critical-stratum bounds.\n8. Produce and independently reproduce a canonical preregistration closure manifest binding task-selection witnesses, heads/trees/binaries, tool hashes, endpoints, schedule, analyzer, resources, and protocol hash.\n9. Complete separate Entire Graph proof: per-repository completeness and task evidence, broader retained full-profile corpora with hardware/RSS/output metadata, and proof-ready agent-value evidence ([master plan](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/master-plan.md:54), [language tiers](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/language-tiers.md:13)).\n\nHistorical design precedent—useful as a template, never as current authority—is in [the archived Graph execution plan](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-GRAPH-EXECUTION-PLAN-2026-07-12.md:121): committed exclusion witness before ranking, no retrieval-informed selection or manual backfill, frozen tooling/configuration, and gates hashed before observing rank or score."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
