{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:34:38.088Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f75dd-7f08-7a03-916a-67a070a6b3b9","author":"/root/cohort_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/cohort_audit\nPayload:\nAudit result: PR #34 cannot yet prove a fresh, repository-disjoint slice. Its selection is deterministic and metadata-only, but it never checks the protected prior-repository exclusion union.\n\nI did not inspect V7 identities, queries, qrels, answers, ranks, scores, or outcomes; I ran no paid command and made no edits.\n\n## Reusable identity-safe machinery\n\n- [graph-exclusion-freeze.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/graph-v8/graph-exclusion-freeze.json) is the key artifact:\n  - SHA-256: `7233b60bac097f014047acbefed947db3b5501976053a4ae575512ddccc71e92`\n  - 1,221 repository HMACs\n  - contains no enumerable repository identities\n  - binds the protected V7 exclusion freeze, burn, and catalog\n  - requires the exact 32-byte, mode-`0600` key whose SHA-256 is recorded in the artifact.\n- [freeze_graph_exclusions_v8.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/freeze_graph_exclusions_v8.py:35) provides:\n  - strict key validation;\n  - canonical GitHub repository normalization;\n  - `HMAC-SHA256(normalized owner/repo)`;\n  - collision and source-binding checks.\n- [construct_graph_holdout_v8.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/construct_graph_holdout_v8.py:293) has the reusable validation pattern:\n  - `_excluded_repositories()` validates exact artifact schema/hash/policy/key;\n  - `select_candidates()` applies HMAC exclusion before deterministic ranking.\n- Tests to reuse as patterns:\n  - `competitive-eval/tools/test_freeze_graph_exclusions_v8.py`\n  - `competitive-eval/tools/test_construct_graph_holdout_v8.py`\n- [sem_v7_artifacts.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/sem_v7_artifacts.py:581) supplies canonical reads and hash checking; [write_new_canonical_json()](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/sem_v7_artifacts.py:697) gives atomic no-overwrite publication.\n\nDo not invoke `construct_graph_holdout_v8.py prepare` for this work: that is V8-specific, requires V8 catalog authorization, and could create V8 candidate material. Extract or wrap only its generic exclusion validation.\n\n## What PR #34 currently lacks\n\n- [construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:35) excludes only two product repos and three prior repair repos. It accepts no HMAC exclusion freeze/key.\n- Selection at [lines 140–167](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:140) simply chooses the minimum salted digest per language, so rerunning it selects the already-observed three repositories.\n- Its test at [lines 65–79](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/test_construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:65) hardcodes those already-run repositories; there is no protected-exclusion test.\n- It self-declares `outcome_data_consulted: false`, but does not bind a filesystem-restricted selection environment or complete input/source closure.\n- It publishes full `candidate_rankings` and cases containing controller expectations/score-artifact paths, rather than separating public questions from sealed qrels.\n- It overwrites with `write_bytes()` rather than using the repository’s no-overwrite artifact primitive.\n- [run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:58) accepts only the two existing development suites and requires `development_only=true`, `confirmatory_use_allowed=false`.\n- Its schedule at [lines 1245–1268](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:1245) records exactly one attempt per repository/system. There are no repeated paired attempts.\n- The execution config binds binaries and heads, but is created inside `run`; there is no freeze-only/preflight stage or separate reviewed authorization that the runner must validate before launching a paid process.\n- This matches the PR’s own warning: [preindexed-agentic-v2/README.md](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/preindexed-agentic-v2/README.md:63) requires a fresh outcome-blind slice, frozen heads, explicit semantics, and repeated paired attempts, and explicitly authorizes no paid rerun.\n\n## Candidate sources\n\n- The authored Tasks corpus is not a fresh repository-level source: there are 164 task files and 164 existing score artifacts. It remains suitable for development regression only.\n- `repos.json`, `repos-heldout.json`, `repos-ts.json`, `repos-py.json`, and `repos-rust.json` are genuinely predefined and compiler-oracle capable, but every set already has corresponding `results*/results.json`; they must not be assumed outcome-fresh. The current oracle overlay also already consumed one Go, TypeScript, and Python entry.\n- The strongest existing metadata-only starting pool is:\n  - `competitive-eval/core-bench/candidate-catalog.json`\n  - pinned CORE-Bench revision `682c1e668692a1f28a3351511d88e71fce2809ef`\n  - pinned Multi-SWE-bench revision `56ff018c04a38e27ada1e9d0a6d5839a51f88f0d`\n  - 35 candidates, 18 eligibility-qualified across seven languages\n  - `spike-manifest.json` previously selected eight, leaving ten eligible-but-unselected at metadata level.\n- `competitive-eval/core-bench/overlap-exclusions.json` adds 307 public exclusions, but is insufficient by itself; the 1,221-entry HMAC union remains mandatory.\n- Reuse the deterministic, language-stratified selection and source-hash patterns in `core_bench_graph_spike.py`, but create a new freezer rather than changing that evidence-bound script.\n\n## Recommended fresh-slice design\n\nCreate a distinct suite such as `entire_graph_agentic_confirmatory_mini_v1` with a preregistered new seed.\n\n1. Build a metadata-only candidate pool from the ten previously unselected CORE-Bench candidates, or a newly pinned external manifest.\n2. Internally normalize and HMAC every candidate with the protected key.\n3. Exclude matches against the committed 1,221-entry union before ranking.\n4. Also exclude all post-freeze PR #34 cohorts: the Tasks smoke, oracle overlay, repair pilot, and any other run completed after the V8 exclusion artifact was frozen.\n5. Emit only:\n   - source manifest hashes and candidate-set hash;\n   - aggregate eligible/excluded counts;\n   - selection seed/rule;\n   - selected nonmatching public repositories;\n   - exclusion-freeze SHA and key SHA.\n   \n   Do not emit which candidate identities matched the protected union.\n6. Freeze public questions separately from controller-only qrels/answers. The public manifest should bind the sealed qrel SHA but contain no expected answers.\n7. Use three repositories across three languages, three systems, and at least three paired repetitions: 27 attempts, balanced/rotated within repository blocks.\n8. Freeze product head, Graph and CBM binaries, Claude/model, runner, scorer, prompt semantics, budgets, and attempt schedule before any paid execution.\n9. Add a preflight command that materializes and validates all checkouts/indexes and stops. Require a separate exact-hash execution authorization before `run`.\n\nRecommended new files:\n\n- `competitive-eval/tools/freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py`\n- `competitive-eval/tools/test_freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py`\n- `competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py`\n- `competitive-eval/agentic-confirmatory-mini-v1/README.md`\n- `candidate-source-freeze.json`\n- `repository-disjointness-attestation.json`\n- `manifest.json` with public questions only\n- protected `sealed-qrels.json`, hash-bound from the manifest\n- `execution-freeze.json`\n- `execution-authorization.json`, initially with paid execution false.\n\nProposed non-paid workflow after implementing the freezer:\n\n```sh\npython3 competitive-eval/tools/freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py freeze \\\n  --candidate-catalog competitive-eval/core-bench/candidate-catalog.json \\\n  --prior-manifest competitive-eval/core-bench/spike-manifest.json \\\n  --exclusions competitive-eval/graph-v8/graph-exclusion-freeze.json \\\n  --exclusion-key /protected/path/repository-identity.key \\\n  --output-dir /private/tmp/agentic-confirmatory-mini-v1-freeze\n\npython3 competitive-eval/tools/freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py validate \\\n  --input-dir /private/tmp/agentic-confirmatory-mini-v1-freeze \\\n  --exclusion-key /protected/path/repository-identity.key\n\npython3 -m pytest -q \\\n  competitive-eval/tools/test_freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py\n```\n\nStop after freeze, validation, commit, and independent review. Do not call the current `run` or `all` commands."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
