{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:46:15.935Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75e8-24ff-7e02-abd5-e4f82f9b3491","call_id":"call_NpbmBaZFa8c1DYyuBrChIUs9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"af7ca6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002583,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3635,\"output\":\"README.md:56:- **🧭 Git-native and reproducible.** Every snapshot is keyed by `(repo, commit, tree)`, so the graph is content-addressed and cacheable per commit. Reads committed `HEAD` by default; pass `--worktree` for live edits.\\nREADME.md:117:| `entire graph index --head --profile full` | Prebuild a durable, query-independent index for committed `HEAD` |\\nREADME.md:119:| `entire graph neighbors --symbol NAME` | Direct graph neighbors and bounded two-hop paths for a symbol |\\nREADME.md:152:entire graph index --repo . --head --profile full --cache-dir /path/to/cache --format json\\nREADME.md:157:use the same repository scope—and therefore the same cache key—as later search\\nREADME.md:160:provider version, and reports `index_cache_hit` plus indexing latency. A\\nREADME.md:161:successful invocation verifies that the compressed cache artifact was written\\nREADME.md:162:durably. Repeat the command to require a cache hit before starting measured or\\nREADME.md:166:entire graph search --repo . --query \\\"retry logic for webhook delivery\\\" --top-k 20 --format agent --head --profile full --index-all-files --cache-dir /path/to/cache\\nREADME.md:171:reparsing), or omit `--head` and the cache flags when the agent must inspect\\nREADME.md:187:- **Agent-native output.** `--format agent` starts with an auditable cache hit/miss line, then emits only ranked locations, symbol names, and focused source, preserving more useful code inside the same budget. Use `json` or `ndjson` when a program needs the full result schema and search diagnostics.\\nREADME.md:191:- **Caching.** When Entire supplies `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`, committed-tree searches reuse a tree-keyed compressed index across invocations. Direct callers can set `--cache-dir`; `--no-cache` disables persistence. A complete cache prepared by `index` also serves selective searches without changing their result set. Worktree searches never reuse committed indexes, avoiding stale results after edits.\\nREADME.md:197:entire graph neighbors --repo . --symbol ExecuteC --file command.go --depth 2 --format agent\\nREADME.md:200:`neighbors` reports resolved incoming and outgoing relations with definition\\nREADME.md:206:removes conventional test-only neighbors, and `--limit` bounds neighbor lists.\\nREADME.md:213:`--cache-dir`; worktree queries bypass that cache so dirty edits stay visible.\\nREADME.md:344:- **Explicit preindex:** `index --head` builds and verifies that same query-independent artifact before latency-sensitive agent work; cached `search` and `neighbors` calls then report the hit directly.\\nREADME.md:372:- `index --head --format json` prepares a complete committed-tree search/neighbor cache and reports exact provenance and cache state.\\nREADME.md:399:| `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` | Enables the tree-keyed compressed index cache for committed-tree index, search, and neighbor queries |\\nREADME.md:403:| `--cache-dir` / `--no-cache` | Set or disable the search index cache directory |\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:43:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-collection-flow -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:44:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-istio-resource-refs -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:45:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-object-literal-flow -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:48:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-array-join-routes -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:51:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-array-join-http-calls -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:55:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-graphql-schema-fields -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:57:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-k8s-namespaced-resource-refs -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:58:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages Go -limit 1 -skip-clone -profile syntax-only -provider-version codex-namespace-refs -min-loc-per-sec 1\\ndocs/validation/full-plan-local-proof-20260620.md:59:go run ./cmd/graph-bench -manifest bench/repos.fast.json -cache bench/.cache -out bench/results -lock bench/repos.lock.json -languages G